/* Troubleshooting. With no router around, a hotspot is the only way */
"trouble.link" = "Can't connect?";
"trouble.title" = "If nothing shows up";
"trouble.same.title" = "1. Are both on the same network?";
"trouble.same.body" = "If the phone is on the 5 GHz band and the computer on 2.4 GHz, some routers keep them apart. Join the same Wi-Fi name on both.";
"trouble.guest.title" = "2. Is it a guest network?";
"trouble.guest.body" = "Office, hotel and cafe networks usually turn on client isolation, which blocks devices from reaching each other. On those, use the hotspot method below.";
"trouble.hotspot.title" = "3. No router: use a personal hotspot";
"trouble.hotspot.body" = "Turn on the hotspot on one device and join it from the other. Both are then on the same network, over a direct link that is usually faster than public Wi-Fi.\n\niPhone: Settings → Personal Hotspot → Allow Others to Join.\nAndroid: Settings → Hotspot & tethering → turn it on.\n\nThe device sharing the hotspot doesn't need Wi-Fi. Nothing goes over cellular data — files travel only between the two devices.";
"trouble.manual.title" = "4. Still nothing: type the address";
"trouble.manual.body" = "Some routers drop the multicast used for discovery even though a direct connection works. Read the address and 6-digit code off the other device and enter them under \"Enter address\".";
